  "notes": "{右折|うせつ} is the formal/technical term for turning right, commonly used in traffic contexts and directions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {右折|うせつ}する: to turn right\n- {右折|うせつ}{禁止|きんし}: no right turn\n- {右折|うせつ}{車線|しゃせん}: right turn lane\n- {右折|うせつ}{専用|せんよう}: right turn only\n\nTRAFFIC NOTES:\n- In Japan, driving is on the left, so {右折|うせつ} crosses oncoming traffic\n- {右折|うせつ} requires extra caution compared to {左折|させつ}\n- Some intersections have {右折|うせつ}{信号|しんごう} (right turn signals)",
